<section class="page-lead page-shell" aria-labelledby="engineering-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Engineering · Public examples</p>
  <h1 id="engineering-title">Different projects make <em>different engineering choices.</em></h1>
  <p class="lead-copy">The public record includes a Rust semantic engine, repository-based state, a local planning store, a native review client, and an offline-first learning application. Private projects have less to show, and their implementation details stay private.</p>
</section>

<section class="engineering-principles page-shell" aria-labelledby="examples-title">
  <div class="section-heading section-heading--stacked">
    <p class="eyebrow">Implementation notes</p>
    <h2 id="examples-title">Decisions visible in the public sources</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="engineering-examples">
    <article class="engineering-example engineering-example--wide">
      <p class="example-label">RepoPact Core · released CLI 3.1.3</p>
      <h3>Rust defines the semantics; the CLI exposes supported operations.</h3>
      <p>Core reads repository records, validates them, and prepares typed operations through a canonical Rust engine. The published Python package provides the command-line surface. Admission checks do not establish arbitrary process confinement; that claim needs operating-system evidence for the specific boundary.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-core/blob/614689b127cf52f801877cc48440f7e45c3709eb/README.md">Read the Core design notes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
    <article class="engineering-example">
      <p class="example-label">RepoPact Workbench · source-build preview</p>
      <h3>A separate client of Core</h3>
      <p>Workbench is a native review application with its own project and release stream. The recorded screenshot uses a disposable Core conformance fixture. No packaged installer is listed; the project’s platform notes bound its recorded checks.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-workbench/tree/414a4a78091796735a1b97b03fd8c3cf1c105f30">Inspect its source and platform notes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
    <article class="engineering-example">
      <p class="example-label">Anvil · developer preview 0.1.0a0</p>
      <h3>Local planning state</h3>
      <p>Anvil stores planning records in a single-writer JSON file and links typed references to external work. Its API and schema may change; it does not own execution or present itself as an audit trail.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/anvil/tree/89ac5df34090e9ffde6a0b790620e9096fb0f15d">Read Anvil’s source documentation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="architecture-study" aria-labelledby="study-title">
  <div class="page-shell study-layout">
    <div class="study-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">RepoPact Core · Architecture</p>
      <h2 id="study-title">Repository records stay authoritative.</h2>
      <p>The CLI and Workbench read governed records and request supported operations from Core. The engine validates the records and prepares plans. Dashboards and graph views are derived surfaces, while the evidence records observed results.</p>
      <p>This is RepoPact Core’s documented architecture. It does not describe ForgeWire, Fabric, Anvil, or ForgeLink.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-core/blob/614689b127cf52f801877cc48440f7e45c3709eb/docs/assets/readme/repopact-architecture.svg">Open the source diagram <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <figure class="architecture-figure architecture-figure--large">
      <img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/repopact-architecture.svg" alt="RepoPact Core architecture: people and client applications interact with the canonical Rust engine; repository records remain authoritative; evidence and derived views record observed or computed information." aria-describedby="engineering-diagram-notes" width="1200" height="720" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>Architecture copied from RepoPact Core’s public documentation. <a href="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/repopact-architecture.svg">Open the full-size image</a>.</figcaption>
      <p class="diagram-notes" id="engineering-diagram-notes"><strong>Diagram key.</strong> Blue arrows mark exchanges with Core. Slate arrows mark human or host interactions, evidence, and derived-view relationships. Dashed boxes are derived views; the host/CI integration is optional and provider-specific.</p>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

